## DESCRIPTION
## Inverse function theorem
## ENDDESCRIPTION

## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Inverse function theorem')

########################################################################

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "parserPopUp.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

##############################################################
#
#  Setup

$mc_yes = PopUp(["?", "Yes", "No"], "Yes");
$mc_no = PopUp(["?", "Yes", "No"], "No");

##############################################################
#
#  Text

BEGIN_PGML


Determine whether the function is a local diffeomorphism at the given point.

1. Let [`F: \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}^2`] be [`C^1`]. If [`DF(0,0) = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 3\\2 & 6 \end{bmatrix}`], is [`F`] a local diffeomorphism at [`(0,0)`]? [_]{$mc_no}

2. Let [`G: \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R}^3`] be [`C^1`]. If [`DG(2,3,7)  = \begin{bmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\0 & 0 & 6 \end{bmatrix}`], is [`G`] a local diffeomorphism at [`(2,3,7)`]? [_]{$mc_yes}

3. Let [`H : \mathbb{R}^{237} \to \mathbb{R}^{237}`] be [`C^1`] and let [`a \in \mathbb{R}^{237}`]. If the differential [`dH_a`]  is injective, then is [`H`] a local diffeomorphism at [`a`]? [_]{$mc_yes}

4. Let [`\phi : \mathbb{R}^{237} \to \mathbb{R}^{237}`] be [`C^1`] and let [`a \in \mathbb{R}^{237}`]. If the differential [`d\phi_a`]  is surjective, then is [`\phi`] a local diffeomorphism at [`a`]? [_]{$mc_yes}
END_PGML

ENDDOCUMENT();